    <selectionEntry id="a9051bcd-cd1b-a2d9-8d54-af5023dfcd0e-29754" name="The Defenders of the Cathedrum" hidden="false" collective="false" type="unit">
      <profiles />
      <rules>
        <rule id="90cfd70f-3d45-a2b5-7ee6-3fb72d23d285-29754" name="Stubborn" hidden="false">
          <profiles />
          <rules />
          <infoLinks />
          <modifiers />
        <description>When taking Morale tests, stubborn units always ignore any negative Leadership modifiers. Independent characters that are stubborn confer the ability onto any unit that they join.</description></rule>
        <rule id="909b9836-4080-e9f2-9943-e563b3369f7f-29754" name="Counter-attack" hidden="false">
          <profiles />
          <rules />
          <infoLinks />
          <modifiers />
        <description>When a unit with this rule is assaulted by the enemy it must take a Leadership test. If the test is successful all models in the unit get the +1 assault bonus to their attacks, exactly as if they too had assaulted that turn.


This rule cannot be used if, when assaulted, the unit was already locked in combat from a previous turn.</description></rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <constraints />
      <selectionEntries />
      <selectionEntryGroups>
